 "sublayer_id": "inference_serving",
 "timing_rationale": "Coincident: revenue moves with the tokens served in the same months, and firms disclose it within weeks when they disclose it at all.",
 "tracker_interpretation": "Several inference platforms report run-rates between a few hundred million and about a billion dollars, growing several-fold in a year, while the price of a token at fixed capability falls; revenue says nothing about their margins, which none publishes.",
 "unit": "USD",
 "unpublished_reason": "No direction rule fits yet: the firms report different measures on irregular dates, so there is no single series to read for a trend. The rows are on /series and in Ask; margins, which would settle whether the layer keeps its rent, are not published by any of them.",
 "updated_at": "2026-09-25",
 "valve_measured": null,
 "why_it_matters": "The serving layer sits between the model makers and the applications; whether it keeps margin as token prices fall decides whether it is a durable business or a pass-through."
